    "#  TRAIN_FRACTIONS uses wider spacing — 10/30/50/70/100 \n",
    "#  Since the moving-frame pool is much smaller than the full raw-frame pool (most frames contain only stationary balls). \n",
    "#  Wider spacing ensures meaningful differences between runs and avoids wasting compute on fractions that are too close together to show a real gap.\n",
